  "latest_findings": {
    "magnetic_baseline": "Coreless/slotless AFPM starter-generator remains the preferred first Axle magnetic machine.",
    "faraday_generator_result": "The transformer analogy is valid only at the shared Faraday-law level. Rotating Axle magnets relative to stationary windings form a generator. The intended harvest path is stationary AFPM windings -> bidirectional inverter -> DC bus -> battery.",
    "bulk_conductor_result": "Eddy currents induced in solid copper/brass Axle material behave like an unintended shorted secondary: they create Lenz drag and heat and are not the preferred collection path.",
    "motor_regen_rule": "Battery-only spin cannot create net gain by regenerating from the same shaft. Genuine regeneration requires independently measured mechanical input or recovery of finite rotor kinetic energy.",
    "automatic_crossover": "During startup AFPM is a motor; hydraulic/external assistance can reduce current toward zero; if external torque exceeds total drag the same AFPM crosses into generator mode and charges the battery.",
    "copper_vs_brass": "Brass-class non-ferromagnetic structural material remains the preliminary electromagnetic preference over solid copper pending matched-geometry field/eddy/corrosion testing.",
    "journal_policy": "JANUS Engine development journal remains append-only and now records the generator/regeneration interpretation."
  },
